 "description": "Follow how my views, my relationships and my place in society develop — keeping every earlier stage.",
 "inspiration": "Original: In the Phenomenology of Spirit, Hegel traces how consciousness develops through experience: each way of understanding meets its limits and is taken up into a richer one. Self-consciousness needs recognition from others, and freedom becomes real in shared life — family, civil society and the state (Philosophy of Right).\n\nMinest adaptation: this template follows that idea of development over time in a personal world. It does not use a fixed “thesis → antithesis → synthesis” formula, which Hegel himself did not use as his method.",
